# Thornvault Forager with Crime Novelist: the Food sacrificed to forage is the cost of a mana ability, so the Novelist's "whenever you
# sacrifice an artifact" is a triggered mana ability (CR 605.1b) and resolves at once, with no stack (CR 605.4a): its counter and {R}
# come with the Forager's two mana. Turn 1: Black Lotus pays for the Novelist, the Forest and a Mox Emerald for the Forager, the other
# Mox for Gilded Goose and its Food. Turn 3: the Forager forages by sacrificing the Food (the graveyard holds only the Lotus, so that is
# the only way) for {G}{G}, and the Novelist's {R} is already in the pool with nothing on the stack.

[Bot1 Deck]
Thornvault Forager
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Gilded Goose
Crime Novelist
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Crime Novelist.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thornvault Forager.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gilded Goose.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Food Token.Subtypes = Food
? Bot1.Battlefield.Crime Novelist.Power = 1
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Thornvault Forager.Activate(Ability: Forage)
Bot1.Colors(Green; Green)
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Food Token = (absent)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Crime Novelist.Power = 2

[Expect]
Bot1.Mana = {R}{G}{G}
Bot1.Battlefield.Crime Novelist.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Thornvault Forager.Tapped = true
